module gunbc.plans.fail_closed_lockdown


fn fail_closed_lockdown_body() -> List<std.markdown.MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Status:** audit + lock-down checklist · **DESIGN.md + carriers are authority** (§6 no parallel ledger); each item dissolves into a wired CI gate when it lands. Linked from `ROADMAP.md §0`."),
    p(text: "**Verified against the live tree 2026-06-21.** Named symbols are receipts; re-check before acting."),
    h2(text: "0. Thesis — three faces of one problem"),
    p(text: "Cache misses/flakes, un-wired lenses, and complexity violations are **the same failure**: a discipline is *modeled* but not **enforced fail-closed, by execution, in CI**. DESIGN §6 names it — *\"the tier where the machinery exists but nothing gates on it\"* (coverage by illusion). The lock-down goal: for every discipline, a fail-open state is **physically impossible to write** because a discovered CI witness goes RED on it. Lock the machine down *before* expanding (the operator's bet: build the efficient correct machine, dogfood daily, sell the pieces — infra/website/billing/backend — once each is locked)."),
    p(text: "The test for \"locked\": (a) wired into the floor (discovered + run), (b) fail-closed (RED on violation, never a warning), (c) green-by-execution with a **discriminating** input that goes RED when wrong."),
    p(text: "**The governing principle is CONSTRUCTION, not validation** — now an axiom in [DESIGN §5](../../DESIGN.md) (lenses are the residue mechanism, §6): make the bad state *unwritable* (single authority / realization derived from model), reserve lenses for the genuinely-unstructurable. #5423's spec-only key lens shipping a false-green is the proof. So §4 below is ordered **construction-first**; the lens items are the residue that survives it. (Construction does *not* evict the executable hygiene backstop — see §4 meta.)"),
    h2(text: "1. What IS enforced fail-closed today (the good baseline)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "Gate"), cell(text: "Scope"), cell(text: "Evidence")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "DagCompileCleanGate"), cell(text: "whole tree (fail-fast root)"), cell(text: "`gunbc.ci_gate` `DagCompileCleanGate`; `v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan` `gate_runnable`")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "GeneratedArtifactDriftGate"), cell(text: "`ci.yml` / `ROADMAP.md` / `.gitignore` byte-drift + per-artifact perturb, over the committed (= generated AND not-ignored) registry"), cell(text: "`gunbc.ci_gate` `GeneratedArtifactDriftGate`; `tools.generated_artifact_gate` `run_generated_artifact_drift_gate`; `gunbc.generated_artifact` `committed_generated_artifacts`")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "These are the **structural** gates. The gap is everything *analytical* and the *bootstrap purity* gate."),
    h2(text: "2. Coverage by illusion — authored but inert / vacuous (fail-open by inertia)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "Lens / gate"), cell(text: "State"), cell(text: "Why it enforces nothing")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**complexity**, **cost**"), cell(text: "inert"), cell(text: "single authority for the §1 time axis; **no `test fn`/gate runs them on the tree** — a mis-costed loop ships silently (`lens/complexity.dag`, `lens/cost.dag`)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**host_language_transport_script**"), cell(text: "LIVE (#7184)"), cell(text: "§5 literal-blob ban — ACTIVATED, no longer inert: a per-PR ReadsLiveTree consumer over the `shell.Exec.Run` anchor sites (`wall_residue_live_test.dag`) reds a NEW raw literal at an enrolled Run position. Deliberately green on `ComputedApplication` (the counted `retained_*` bridge calls), so it backstops literal blobs only. CONSTRUCTION now closes BOTH edges: `ShellOnHost.script` is the `RetainedShellScript` record, and `TransportScript` itself is a `sole_constructor` record whose only mint (`extdeps.shell.exec` `transport_script_seal`) is `admit_callers`-sealed, so a bare `String`, a computed join and an `as TransportScript` cast are all unwritable at a direct `shell.Exec.Run` position too. The lens is therefore a REGRESSION control over a class construction now owns, not the wall — it stays enrolled precisely so the higher rung is proven to hold (DESIGN 4b: a climb deletes the redundant production machinery, never the evidence). Corrected 2026-07-27: this row said the record closed the `shell.Exec.Run` computed-join class, but that wall was then scoped to `ShellOnHost`; the sole-constructor wall is what closed the remaining half.")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**leaf_model_verification**"), cell(text: "inert"), cell(text: "845-line R1–R3 realization matrix; test data never discovered")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**extdeps_shape_transport_policy**"), cell(text: "inert"), cell(text: "the §3 shape/transport/policy enforcer — authored, not wired")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "affected_set, fact_cardinality, mock_totality, ownership, subsumption, …"), cell(text: "inert"), cell(text: "authored lenses, no discovered gate")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**discrimination, synthesis, idempotency, parallelism**"), cell(text: "advisory / roster"), cell(text: "run, but over a **curated roster**, not the change-set — a violation outside the roster merges (`lens_*_family_eval_test.dag`)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**EmitHostGate**"), cell(text: "wired but thin"), cell(text: "exactly **4 MVP fixtures** (rust/python/go/ts), not the emit tree (`tools.floor_effect_gate_witness` `emit_host_gate_passes`)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "**regen_stage0 --verify** (Stage0LockstepGate)"), cell(text: "**not wired**"), cell(text: "exists (`verify_stage0_matches`), absent from the floor → seed hand-drift uncaught; gate sits in **closed #5325**")]),
      ],
    },
    h2(text: "3. Where the pipeline actually fails OPEN (wrong answer passes silently)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "Site"), cell(text: "Class"), cell(text: "What it fabricates / masks")]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "`v1_interpreter.rs` `pure_call_memo_key`"), cell(text: "key-by-address"), cell(text: "keys on `Rc::as_ptr`, not content → stale hit on realloc; structurally-equal args miss")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "`v1_interpreter.rs` `eval_record_lit`"), cell(text: "fail-open infer"), cell(text: "`record_lit_type_name_at(..).unwrap_or_default()` → `\"\"` type instead of error")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [cell(text: "`v1_interpreter.rs` `dispatch_shell`, `eval_service_call`"), cell(text: "fail-open IO"), cell(text: "`from_utf8_lossy` / `unwrap_or_default` fabricate plausible text from malformed output")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "**Warm==cold coverage is incomplete, not absent everywhere.** `v2.test.long.parse_table_memo_governed_witness` `parse_table_memo_warm_equals_cold_content_hash` covers the parse-table memo, and `resolve_typed_cache_equivalence_test.rs` `typed_module_cache_matches_cold_oracle_in_every_order` covers the typed-module cache. Resolved-graph disk decoding is fail-closed: `resolved_graph_cache.rs` `read_cached_header` rejects malformed header digests directly; `read_cached_file` cannot accept its empty decode sentinel as either the validated subject digest or computed payload digest, witnessed by `resolve_cross_process_cache_test.rs` `poisoned_hit_rejected_on_subject_digest_mismatch`. The provider additionally refuses where it cannot expose a faithful probe (`resolved_graph_cache.rs` `faithful_probe_unavailable_gap`). `pure_call_memo` still lacks a warm==cold oracle, leaving its address-keyed flake surface concrete."),
    p(text: "Already fixed (precedent for the pattern): cross-representation `==` straddle (now raises `CrossRepresentationEquality`); strict record-field typecheck (#5293)."),
    h2(text: "3a. How deep does the root go — the remaining audits"),
    p(text: "§1–§3 were the first two passes (lens wiring + fail-open code). They found *symptoms*. The lane needs deeper audits before we trust the fixes are complete, because the symptoms likely share **one root**."),
    p(text: "**Suspected root — the model↔realization fork (DESIGN open thread, §1/§2/§7).** Every primitive is *modeled* as a coproduct and *realized* as a native `Value`, reconciled by **per-site bridges** — so coverage is accidental and non-compositional. That is the same shape as the `==` straddle (`Value::eq` `_ => false`) and the under-keyed pure-call memo (native address vs modeled content identity). If true, the fixes in §4 are *per-site patches* unless the root is dissolved (ground each primitive into its realization — numeric tower first, `Int = GroupCompletion<Nat>` bottoming in Peano `Nat`), which makes whole classes of guard *dead code*."),
    p(text: "Audits to run (each: how many sites, how deep, is there one root):"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**model↔realization fork audit** — ✅ DONE → [model-realization-fork.md](model-realization-fork.md). ROOT CONFIRMED (one seam, ~13 per-site bridges). Two sub-roots: numeric tower (grounds cleanly → guard dead code) + `Value::Null` overload (None/Absent/miss/Violates — needs *splitting*, the deeper root; ~131 legitimate `present==None→false` sites mean it can't be guarded)."),
      li(text: "**coercion/equality fail-closure audit** — the `==` fix landed for the numeric tower; remaining: `Bool True|False` over `Value::Bool`, `Optional/Witness` over the overloaded `Value::Null` sentinel (resists a blanket guard — `present == None` at ~131 sites is a *legitimate* `false`; needs grounding)."),
      li(text: "**inference fail-open audit** — what remains after strict record-field (#5293): return-type inference defaults, other `unwrap_or_default` type fabrications."),
      li(text: "**cache-purity audit** — enumerate every cache (resolved_graph, parse_table_memo, pure_call_memo, typed_module, sccache); each must have a warm==cold oracle or fail-closed refusal. Coverage exists for typed_module (`resolve_typed_cache_equivalence_test.rs` `typed_module_cache_matches_cold_oracle_in_every_order`) and parse_table_memo (`v2.test.long.parse_table_memo_governed_witness` `parse_table_memo_warm_equals_cold_content_hash`); resolved_graph refuses the unavailable faithful probe (`resolved_graph_cache.rs` `faithful_probe_unavailable_gap`); pure_call_memo remains uncovered."),
      li(text: "**CI-coverage-completeness audit** — tests/gates that *exist but don't run*. Confirmed historical instance: the now-retired Rust monolith gate (`gunbc.commit_workflow` `commit_gate_rust_suite_removed_disposition`; local-only implementation `tools.rust_gates_ci` `run_rust_monolith_gate`) admitted a narrow subset of the `src/v1/tests` corpus — the rest could rot silently (how the Behavior-arm test went stale). Also: the `discrimination` lens (the §5 discriminating-witness enforcer) is itself roster-only, not whole-corpus — the enforcer is vacuous."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The lane is done when these audits return *no new fail-open class* and §4 is green."),
    p(text: "**Deepest recursion (DESIGN open thread #1) — lock down the reasoning, not just the code.** The same fail-closed discipline applies to the *argument*: model A1–A3 + the §1–§7 chain in `.dag` and have a lens enforce the syllogism — every claim a consequence-chain back to an axiom, **no orphan, no cycle** (the §4 acyclicity test turned on this document; the §7 recursion). Currently not modeled at all (grep empty). This is the apex lock-down: a design claim with no axiom-chain is an orphan = should be RED."),
    h2(text: "4. Lock-down checklist (blocks expansion)"),
    p(text: "Two tiers: **construction** (the class becomes unwritable — this is the real work) then **lens** (the residue that genuinely can't be made impossible by construction). The cache items are the operator's top priority."),
    p(text: "**Tier 1 — construction (make the class unwritable):**"),
    tasks(items: [
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Dissolve the model↔realization fork — THE root** ([model-realization-fork.md](model-realization-fork.md)): realization derived from model. (1) numeric tower `Int=GroupCompletion<Nat>` → the `==` straddle guard becomes dead code; (2) split `Value::Null` (None/Absent/miss/Violates → own carriers)."),
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Cache key derived FROM declared `inputs_considered`** (single authority) → cannot declare an input you don't key, nor key one you don't declare; divergence unwritable. Subsumes a content key for `pure_call_memo` (kill the address key). *(worked first instance: child adhoc-cc232dbc-1be)*"),
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Self-host purity by construction** — emitter emits the whole seed so `patch_*`/`HAND_MAINTAINED_STAGE0_FILES` are unwritable; `regen_stage0 --verify` (Stage0LockstepGate, #5325) then a residue check."),
      task(state: Checked, text: "**Rust monolith gate retired.** `gunbc.commit_workflow` `commit_gate_rust_suite_removed_disposition` records the terminal retirement: nextest remains local and leaves with the v1 seed; required CI separately retains formatting and compile-only coverage, without re-enrolling the monolith."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Tier 2 — lens (only the genuinely-unstructurable residue; each must justify why not construction):**"),
    tasks(items: [
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Complexity / cost / necessity** — legitimate lens (can't structurally forbid an *unnecessary* loop); fix cost-lens zero-absorption (`symbolic_max` floor), then gate the change-set (not a roster) → §6."),
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Cache-redundancy completeness** (§7 P3) — shared-across-boundary → ERROR; reach, not measurement; the residue that survives the content-key construction."),
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**warm==cold purity-oracle witness per cache** — residue check behind the content-key construction (guaranteed once the key is fn-of-inputs, but cheap to witness)."),
      task(state: Unchecked, text: "**Promote-or-delete every inert lens** (extdeps_shape_transport_policy, leaf_model_verification, …; host_language_transport_script is DONE — promoted live by #7184); de-vacuum thin gates (EmitHostGate beyond 4 fixtures; advisory rosters → change-set); the `discrimination` enforcer is itself roster-only — whole-corpus it."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Meta — two layers, the executable one is load-bearing:**"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**inert-lens hygiene (executable backstop):** every `lens/*.dag` has a discovered fail-closed witness, or is **removed** — an inert lens is a lie. This *runs* over the corpus and is the thing that actually closes the \"authored ≠ enforced\" loophole."),
      li(text: "**construction-justification rule (layered ON TOP, authoring-time judgment):** before adding any lens, justify why the class can't be made impossible by construction; convert what can (single authority / realization-from-model); lens-justify only the unstructurable residue. This is a better *principle* but does **not** supersede the executable backstop — a judgment applied at authoring time executes nothing, so it cannot replace a check that runs over the corpus."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data fail_closed_lockdown_plan: gunbc.plan.Plan = gunbc.plan.Plan {
  slug: "fail-closed-lockdown",
  title: "Plan — Fail-closed lock-down (make fail-open physically impossible to write)",
  body: fail_closed_lockdown_body(),
  retirement: gunbc.plan.PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the §4 checklist is green: every discipline has a discovered, fail-closed, discriminating CI witness, and the meta-invariant gate exists so a new inert lens cannot be added. At that point the floor *is* the lock-down and this audit is redundant.")
  }
}
